      ":question/worked-solution": "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-6,-3).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-6$ and $y=-3$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\ 9 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-\\frac{3}{2}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{3}{2}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{3}{4y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard"
